  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "ANOVA uses sums of squares, the derivation of which we outline below. Throughout, we use SS to denote an observed sum of squares, and $ E(\\mathrm{SS}) $ to denote its expected value. As we will see shortly, scaled sums of squares, known as mean squares, are used to estimate variance components. We use the parallel notation, MS and $ E(\\mathrm{MS}) $, to denote observed and expected mean squares.",
      "source_page": 570,
      "printed_page": 550,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter18:p004:b7",
        "Genetics_chapter18:p004:b8"
      ],
      "bbox": [
