    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "defines the observed total sum of squares around the grand mean $ \\overline{z} $. ANOVA partitions $ SS_{T} $ into components describing variation among the $ s_{i} $ (i.e., among families) and among the $ e_{ij} $ within families. This partitioning is readily accom- plished by expanding around the observed family means, $ \\overline{z}_{i} = \\sum_{j=1}^{n} z_{ij}/n $,",
      "source_page": 570,
      "printed_page": 550,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter18:p004:b12",
        "Genetics_chapter18:p005:b2"
