    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The within-family sum of squares $ (SS_{e}) $ is simply the sum of the squared deviations of individual measures from their observed family means, while the among-family sum of squares $ (SS_{s}) $ is the sum (over all progeny) of the squared deviations of observed family means from the grand mean.",
      "source_page": 571,
      "printed_page": 551,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter18:p005:b8"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
