      "content_sha256": "fd98be2e27769f5386bc94921e10b8a4473b2ee7591d30474edd6b8bae825386"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Assuming that the parents are a random sample of the population at large, the sums of squares can be used to obtain unbiased estimates of the within- and among-family components of variance in the following way. We note first that the expected within-family sum of squares is",
      "source_page": 571,
      "printed_page": 551,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter18:p005:b9"
      ],
      "bbox": [
