    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "This result follows from the fact that $ \\sum_{j=1}^{n}(z_{ij} - \\overline{z}_{i})^{2}/(n - 1) $ is an unbiased estimate of the variance among sibs in the ith family (Chapter 2) and from our assumption that the variance within each family is equal to $ \\sigma_{e}^{2} $.",
      "source_page": 571,
      "printed_page": 551,
