      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Ratios of quantities estimated with sampling error are usually biased with respect to their parametric values (Appendix 1), and this is true for the intraclass correlation (Ponzoni and James 1978, Wang et al. 1991). Letting $ \\tau $ be the parametric value, the downward bias is approximately",
